---
description: Prefer git restore when undoing uncommitted agent edits
alwaysApply: true
---

# Undo local work

If the user asks to drop or undo recent agent edits and those changes are **still uncommitted**, prefer `git restore <paths>` (or `git checkout -- <paths>`) over manually reversing the diff. Do not invent a compensating edit when git can put the files back exactly.

Only use destructive git commands (`reset --hard`, etc.) when the user explicitly asks for them.
